cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or build on these experiments, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "ITASORL: Incidental Detection of Surrogate Worlds by a From-Scratch Digital Organism"
authors:
  - family-names: "Tate"
    given-names: "Levy"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0009-1337-0709"
repository-code: "https://github.com/iLevyTate/ItaSoRL"
license: MIT
version: 1.0.0
abstract: >-
  ITASORL measures whether a recurrent agent trained from scratch, with no
  imported semantic knowledge and no reward for detection, comes to carry in its
  state whether its world runs on authentic base dynamics or a substrate-flawed
  surrogate, set against how detectable the flaw is to a privileged detector at a
  stated detector-side noise. Hand-authored flaws (L1 discretization, L2 rollout
  drift) are detectable but did not meet the registered encoding criterion; at
  the L3 gate's detector noise the L2 flaws read 0.62 to 0.65, so the matched
  contrast is L1 against L3. A learned-dynamics fingerprint (L3) met the
  decodability clauses for survival-trained agents carrying a
  next-observation auxiliary at the registered 300-update budget, with the trainer corrected in
  October 2026 (0.733 against 0.589 for a prediction-only arm; the L0 gate open
  on the registered evaluation-world pair and equivalent to chance across eight
  independent pairs). Without the auxiliary the arm reads 0.613 at 300 updates
  and 0.685 at 450, so the auxiliary result is bounded by budget. At matched
  evaluation input a prediction-trained trunk reads the world as well as the
  survival trunk: the signal rides on the trajectories the foraging policy
  produces and is kept by a trunk shaped by next-observation prediction. A
  hand-authored, temporally coherent drag of matched one-step size is read
  through the same direction while white jitter is not, so nothing here is
  specific to learned dynamics. A common-garden control passes its frozen rule
  on the historical agents (0.666, 0.684): prefix condition
  remains decodable after restoring authentic dynamics, and on the corrected agents that is
  carried mostly by the physical footprint of the prefix, not by memory (see
  FINDINGS section 10.6.1 and 17.7). Corrections and what each does not
  establish: docs/CORRECTIONS.md.
keywords:
  - artificial-life
  - reinforcement-learning
  - self-supervised-learning
  - simulation-hypothesis
  - world-models
